---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import DocsNavigation from '../components/DocsNavigation.astro';
import Drawing from '../components/Drawing.astro';
import Mark from '../components/Mark.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import home from '../generated/home.json';
import { installs } from '../lib/home';
import { repositoryUrl } from '../lib/site';

const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'how-it-works', text: 'How it works' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'in-your-app', text: 'limu in your app' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'explore', text: 'Explore' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'limu-and-pele', text: 'limu and Pele' },
];

const explore = [
  { href: '/examples', title: 'Examples', text: 'Every type of diagram limu supports, in each of its themes.' },
  { href: '/playground', title: 'Playground', text: 'Write a diagram and see it laid out as you type.' },
  { href: '/getting-started', title: 'Getting started', text: 'Lay out your first diagram and render it as SVG.' },
  { href: '/theming', title: 'Theming', text: 'Change colors with themes and overrides, or draw parts yourself.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout markdownPath="/index.md">
  <main id="top" class="docs-page home-page">
    <SiteHeader current="introduction" headings={headings} />
    <div class="docs-layout home-layout">
      <DocsNavigation class="docs-toc" current="introduction" headings={headings} />
      <div class="home-content">
        <section class="hero">
          <Mark size={88} />
          <h1 class="lede">limu is a diagram layout engine in Go. It reads Mermaid and leaves the drawing to your program.</h1>
        </section>

        <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="how-it-works">
          <h2 id="how-it-works">How it works</h2>
          <p>Mermaid and Pele lay out a diagram and write it as SVG for a browser to draw.</p>
          <figure class="diagram-figure">
            <figcaption>A renderer of SVG</figcaption>
            <Drawing drawing={home.renderer} label="Mermaid text goes to a layout, then to SVG, then to a browser." />
          </figure>
          <p>limu stops one step earlier, at the scene. A scene is the laid-out diagram as data. It says what each part is and where it goes, but not how it looks. A backend then draws it, whether that is limumygo on the GPU, the svg package, or one you write.</p>
          <figure class="diagram-figure home-figure-limu">
            <figcaption>limu</figcaption>
            <Drawing drawing={home.limu} label="Mermaid text goes to a layout, then to a scene, which MyGo, SVG, or a backend of your own draws." />
          </figure>
          <p>Because the scene holds no colors, switching themes redraws it without laying it out again. An app can also ask the scene which part is under the pointer.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="in-your-app">
          <h2 id="in-your-app">limu in your app</h2>
          <div class="segmented-control home-tabs" style={`--segment-count: ${installs.length}`} role="group" aria-label="Backend">
            {installs.map(({ id, title }, index) => (
              <button type="button" data-install-tab={id} aria-pressed={index === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'} aria-controls={`install-${id}`}>{title}</button>
            ))}
          </div>
          {installs.map(({ id, command, note, code }, index) => (
            <div class="home-install" id={`install-${id}`} data-install-panel={id} hidden={index !== 0}>
              <CodeBlock language="shell" code={command} />
              <p>{note}</p>
              <CodeBlock language="go" code={code} />
            </div>
          ))}
        </section>

        <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="explore">
          <h2 id="explore">Explore</h2>
          <nav class="guide-links" aria-label="Pages to start from">
            {explore.map(({ href, title, text }) => (
              <a class="guide-link-card" href={href}>
                <h3>{title}</h3>
                <p>{text}</p>
              </a>
            ))}
          </nav>
        </section>

        <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="limu-and-pele">
          <h2 id="limu-and-pele">limu and Pele</h2>
          <p>Most of limu is ported function by function from <a href="https://pele.run" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pele</a>, the small, fast Mermaid renderer made by the <a href="https://obsidian.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Obsidian</a> team. limu’s tests check that its layouts match Pele’s number for number. limu is <a href={repositoryUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">open source</a> under the MIT license.</p>
          <p>Pele is named after the goddess of Hawaiʻi’s volcanoes. Limu is the Hawaiian word for the algae in its seas, and this site takes its colors from limu kohu, a red alga that grows in tide pools.</p>
        </section>

        <SiteFooter />
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  const tabs = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-install-tab]');
  const panels = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-install-panel]');
  tabs.forEach((tab) => {
    tab.addEventListener('click', () => {
      tabs.forEach((other) => other.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(other === tab)));
      panels.forEach((panel) => { panel.hidden = panel.dataset.installPanel !== tab.dataset.installTab; });
    });
  });
</script>
